  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3edf825c44ba8994197fd4cca4373a22, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Hello again,


    Lin Wei writing. I read that your shop has more
    regulars now. Regulars are the true reputation of a kitchen.


    Roast duck
    was the dish my old chef never let me touch. For three years I only watched.
    When he finally let me roast one, he said nothing, ate a piece, and walked away.
    The next morning my name was on the duck schedule.


    Brush the skin with
    honey, let it dry, and roast until it crackles. Patience is the main ingredient.


    Some
    approval is quiet. Learn to hear it.'
